WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.670
- [Narrator] When billionaire
Elon Musk bought Twitter,

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.280
some Tesla investors
worried Musk was abandoning

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.540
the electric vehicle maker

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.625
to focus on the social media company.

00:00:08.625 --> 00:00:09.458
(Musk laughing)

00:00:09.458 --> 00:00:10.860
- So in Twitter...

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.182
- What could possibly go wrong?

00:00:12.182 --> 00:00:14.100
(all laughing)

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.960
- [Narrator] Since the deals
closed in late October,

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.380
Tesla shares have slipped
ending the year down 65%.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.840
The company's worst year on record.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.870
But the reason for the selloff
goes far beyond Twitter.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.660
Here's what drove Tesla
investors away in 2022,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.200
and what's affecting the
car maker going into 2023.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.300
Let's start with demand.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.730
For years, Tesla has
stood out as the leader

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.320
in the electric vehicle space,

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.910
and while its dominance continued

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.710
in the third quarter of 2022,

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.530
its market share slipped to 61%.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.430
- In the last year,

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:49.430
we've seen an explosion of
competing EV models for Tesla,

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.700
and as that number continues
to grow over the years,

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.260
the concern is whether or not demand

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.210
for Tesla vehicles will
continue to stay as high

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.470
as it has been in the past.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.730
- [Narrator] According to JD Power,

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.580
there were 33 EV models
available in the US

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:06.330
at the end of 2021, but by the end of 2022

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.270
that number had jumped to 53 models.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.010
Tesla still held four

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:13.199
of the top five selling
EVs last year according

00:01:13.199 --> 00:01:15.120
to S&amp;P Global Mobility.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.100
But the sell-off in Tesla shares

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.018
reflects investors' fear
that its hold won't last

00:01:20.018 --> 00:01:22.350
as newer models arrive.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.840
- Tesla has sold the same
sort of handful of models

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.880
for years now, and the question is

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.400
will Tesla continue to be as competitive

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.040
as it has in the past or
will they become outdated?

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.360
- [Narrator] Further fueling concerns

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.760
are customer wait times for Tesla cars,

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.280
which dropped sharply over 2022.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.200
Some investors see this as a sign

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.091
demand is already softening.

00:01:42.091 --> 00:01:43.740
Musk addressed these concerns

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.810
on Tesla's third quarter earnings call.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.700
- [Musk] I can't emphasize enough.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.690
We have excellent demand for Q4,

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.970
and we expect to sell
every car that we make

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.230
as far into the future as we can see.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:01:59.940
- [Narrator] And in December, the CEO said

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.510
on a Twitter Spaces call
that demand pressures

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:06.030
were driven by rising
interest rate policies.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.340
Production disruptions also contributed

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.960
to the stock slide last year

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.400
leading to Tesla missing

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.710
its full year vehicle delivery target.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.950
The EV makers said it
delivered 1.3 million vehicles

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.130
in 2022, up 40% from 2021.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:22.260
That was shy of its goal
of increasing deliveries

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.670
by 50% or more.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:27.480
It would've needed more than
1.4 million to hit that target.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.640
News of the shortfall pushed stocks down

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.040
another 12% to start the new year.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.520
Its largest single day decline
in more than two years.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.870
Intermittent factory closures

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.420
at Tesla's China plant,
its largest by volume,

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.100
were one part of the problem.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.200
- China's zero COVID policy led

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.900
to a number of shutdowns
at its factory in Shanghai,

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.570
which obviously created
supply issues of its own.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.670
- [Narrator] Tesla also
faced issues at new factories

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.810
in Texas and Germany,

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.730
where it struggled to ramp up production.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.370
Musk addressed those
problems in a May interview.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.920
- Both Berlin and Austin factories

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.670
are gigantic money furnaces right now.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.560
- [Narrator] Rising
supplier and logistics costs

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.120
combined with soaring inflation

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.460
contributed to these production setbacks.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:12.210
- Tesla and every manufacturer
making EVs today is

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:15.540
confronting rapidly rising
costs from the raw materials

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.420
that go into the batteries,
to construction related costs

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.490
or frankly even labor related costs.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:21.782
All of that is going up,

00:03:21.782 --> 00:03:26.670
and the car industry is not
one with huge profit margins.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.740
- [Narrator] For Tesla, this
included spending roughly

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.380
11 billion in the first quarter on items

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.270
needed to make and sell cars.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:35.410
- Overwhelmingly, our concern is how do we

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.130
keep the factories operating

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.100
so we can pay people and not go bankrupt?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.070
- [Narrator] Overvaluation is
another factor some investors

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.840
and analysts say is complicating

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.760
Tesla's shrinking stock price.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.250
- Tesla has been egregiously overvalued

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:53.130
for the last couple years based on hype.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.840
- [Narrator] At its peak,
Tesla was worth more

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.573
than the 10 largest automakers
on the planet combined

00:03:57.573 --> 00:04:00.630
despite having just a
fraction of their sales.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:04.530
- A lot of investors who
have debated whether or not

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:08.010
Tesla is an overvalued
company have done so

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.160
based on the fact that it
owned a huge percentage

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.720
of the US EV market

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:15.210
and that it was the first
mover in that market.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.985
Its valuation was driven
in part by its CEO

00:04:17.985 --> 00:04:20.160
and some investors say Musk's promises

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.710
about future vehicles
have pushed shares higher

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:26.040
though many of the cars
didn't come until years later.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.680
The latest example, Tesla's cyber truck,

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.570
which was first unveiled three years ago

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.340
and still hasn't hit the market.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:33.780
- Cyber truck is gonna be awesome.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.564
It's worth the wait. Believe me.

00:04:35.564 --> 00:04:37.080
- [Narrator] And more directly,

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.481
Musk's move to offload
billions in Tesla stock

00:04:39.481 --> 00:04:41.490
in part related to Twitter,

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.950
has pushed down Tesla's share price.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.860
- Anytime anybody sells $40
billion worth of company's stock

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.200
it's gonna bring that stock price down.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:53.040
What isn't clear is how
that specific action

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.080
is influencing other investors.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.900
- [Narrator] Tesla did not
respond to request for comment.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:01.080
Tesla's stock selloff comes
as investors across the market

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.780
prepare for what some see
as an oncoming recession.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.910
A downturn could slow car buying,

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.130
especially for pricier vehicles.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:13.130
- Will those people who might
otherwise in 2022 or 2021,

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.910
purchase a $60,000 vehicle?

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:19.080
Will they instead purchase a
$40,000 gas powered vehicle?

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.730
- [Narrator] On Tesla's
third quarter earnings call,

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:22.830
Musk said that he sees the EV company

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.570
as recession resilient.

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:28.500
- [Musk] Let's say 2023 is
a brutal recession year.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:32.130
Even then, we generate meaningful cash.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.110
- [Narrator] Tesla investors
are now waiting for later

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:36.120
this month when the car maker will report

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.670
its full year earnings,
which could give a glimpse

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:40.746
of the stock's prospects
for the coming year.

00:05:40.746 --> 00:05:43.413
(upbeat music)

